  <ym-title|Actual mixed marked compiler \V author
  draft><label|actual-mixed-marked-compiler--author-draft>

  Session: independent-review-20261111, bounded authorship delegated by
  coordinator under issue 26 claim expiring 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC. Source
  revision <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. This unit is
  authored by the reviewer agent and requires the parent's independent
  review. No self-approval or review metadata change.

  Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-mixed-marked-compiler.tex>.

  <section|Exact source route inspected><label|exact-source-route-inspected>

  All declarations below are at the pinned revision. Full reads were made
  unless a subset is specified.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.billing_X>,
    <verbatim|v_ceremony>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/West/PayW.lean>: same
    Whip allocation, exact upper and lower calls, TimeBand specialization
    from its uniform interval quantifiers, actual budget equality and
    tickets. This is the endpoint being reconstructed; it is not assumed as a
    proof premise.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|galaFt>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/West/Muse.lean>: arbitrary finite arity,
    same compiler, old ordinary family plus halo/complement family, exact
    upper multipliers and prices, whole-mode leading projection.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|daypay_>, <verbatim|shutters_>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Soft/Crowns.lean>:
    probability bound at coarse coupling, lower ordinary-only family, empty
    leading predicate. <verbatim|gala_> was also read but its arity\<less\>=2
    restriction is not used for the upper all-arity route.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|so_mat>, <verbatim|v_reward>,
    <verbatim|Soft/Agate.lean>: BodyGrant is for genuine fine P; ReturnTrip
    is for white P with the SAME corrected body packets and same loading.
    Exact site price delta+wilt(B)(L^4 T eta)+wilt(B)(g a), marker price T
    eta+a, repair price exp(Sigma)-1+k. No BodyGrant on white P is
    substituted.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Display.Docking.{Towering,forsaken,Parachute,penny,lent,price_wave,accum,price_lift,packs_lift}>,
    <verbatim|Pricetags.lean>: support exponent
    <verbatim|increment(e)=ucap(e)+2=e+7>, salary <verbatim|exp(15^4(e+7))>,
    fine-to-coarse parent multiplicity only for site budget. Source source
    exponents sigma_f are retained and not silently equated with e.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|Holdings>, <verbatim|Spot>,
    <verbatim|bond_cost>, <verbatim|Payout.lean>: actual product inflation,
    per-marker price, actual global forced vs masked regular pointwise
    bounds.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Display.{LetterCost,Shadow,tune,solo,refund}>,
    <verbatim|Dockets.lean>: all three cases of connected integral payment
    including rare-event shadow, integrable positive-weight envelope and
    absence of background packets without body packets.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|Reparations>, <verbatim|learned_club>,
    <verbatim|finances>, <verbatim|Iced.lean>: hole and boundary corrections
    separately, tag average, raw regular/forced and marker budgets. The
    manuscript proves the finite distinct-letter tree bound directly; it does
    not misidentify the repeated-label logarithm bound with this stage.

    <item>Same Docking namespace <verbatim|bead>, <verbatim|acts>,
    <verbatim|pains>, <verbatim|lampBead>, <verbatim|enlightens>,
    <verbatim|purchases>, <verbatim|Snap.lean>: actual masked field evaluated
    on actual fine chart, exact Gamma+(1-Gamma) marker identity, rare-event
    estimate and two copies of the leading price.

    <item>Same Docking namespace <verbatim|TimeBand>, <verbatim|pedestals>,
    <verbatim|fuel>, <verbatim|noInflate>, <verbatim|pass_line>,
    <verbatim|Chimes.lean>: e0 and load=e0+2, K=H^-1/8, firstN=H^-3, z upper
    H^-4 or lower H^-1/2, forced eta=gas(y) or z*w(y), upper multiplier
    gas(x)^-2, lower gas(y)^-1. Uniformity in x,y in [s/2,s], finite arity
    chosen before final threshold.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Flux.{Pertains,ancestor_P,valve}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Flux/Grader.lean>; <verbatim|Risible> in
    <verbatim|Grain.lean>; <verbatim|anchor_tag> in <verbatim|Radar.lean>:
    reader label multiplicity n, distinct from L^4 fine-parent multiplicity,
    exact smallness (2B+1)^4 Sigma\<less\>=1.
    <verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Thirst.{book_site,welter,fel,wilt,range_wilt}> in
    <verbatim|Scatter.lean>: explicit anchor-to-site cost.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.{s_lit_check_ft,s_in_stalls_ft}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/West/Moon.lean>: same leading alphabet
    embedding, finite product integrability, slice radius A B/(3+2n),
    condition 6n+3\<less\>=A/(3+2n), exact all-mode planted projection.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|Kiln>, <verbatim|stove>,
    <verbatim|Soft/Unlid.lean> first 62 lines: compiler chosen before marker
    sets, all-hole/forced embedding for same body alphabet, monotonicity of
    the purchased multipliers. <verbatim|Soft/Bonfire.lean> and
    <verbatim|Soft/Funds.lean> fully read for actual scalar loading and
    unmarked construction. These show where the primitive purchases belong,
    without reclassifying their interfaces as proofs of analytical estimates.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Display.ReturnTrip>,
    <verbatim|auditioned>, <verbatim|clicked>, <verbatim|Revival.lean>: exact
    all-deleted-support identity and full empty-marker embedding. Canonical
    allarity-planted-compiler already proves its extension to marked
    families.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Reuse and remaining boundary><label|reuse-and-remaining-boundary>

  Uses canonical restarted-rank-history, inherited-activity-prices,
  allarity-planted-compiler, allarity-marked-propagation, and the already
  proved sector/forest/exclusion machinery. It supplies actual three-family
  integral pricing, cover/anchor/marker currency, upper/lower scalar
  purchases, same-cell exact selection and genuine-P/white-P normalization
  join. The exact body-product and all-hole compiler purchases must still be
  bound to their actual corrected alphabet and coarse representation on the
  chosen history. The common warning estimate must hold on the actual sector
  measure. This unit does not produce those by assuming only a Gaussian
  covariance, nor manufacture a new history. No claim that reader covariance
  comparison or its primitive field estimates follow from the price assembly.

  Literature/navigation: searched repository literature/reference paths; only
  manuscript/references.bib is present in this clone. No external theorem is
  needed for the displayed finite algebra, nonnegative rooted-tree iteration,
  or elementary exponential estimates. Canonical source-specific proofs are
  reused instead of an unrelated model.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Live issue 26 comments reread; latest checkpoint states unchanged
    confirmed expiry above.

    <item><verbatim|git diff --check>: run, no diagnostics before final
    review submission.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py>: run in this isolated
    clone; fails on missing coordinator-owned
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>, unchanged integration
    limitation.

    <item>No Lean or TeX build, no source edits, no fresh axiom audit. Prose
    remains draft pending parent's independent mathematical/source review.
  </itemize-minus>

  Parent independent review corrections: the covering number is the connected
  covering number used in the canonical inherited-activity-prices unit; both
  budget radii and the block side are positive integers. The final block
  purchase explicitly requires a positive fixed incoming support exponent, or
  the displayed larger purchase inequality, and makes no existence claim at
  zero exponent. Nonnegative estimates are first on finite subfamilies and
  pass to the full alphabet by monotone convergence. These are author
  repairs, not self-approval.

  Final source-precision correction: Chimes.TimeBand uses distinct Tailprice
  inputs. The lower cover purchase is 10<em|15^4(e0+7)\<less\>=L>sigma_lower
  with sigma_lower=e0; the upper is 10<em|15^4(e0+9)\<less\>=L>sigma_upper
  with sigma_upper=e0+2. The manuscript no longer treats the stronger
  common-exponent purchase as the exact selected input.

